  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration found is config_012 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) at 0.7250 accuracy. All four scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer combinations have been tested, confirming scvi_n200 and imagenet_vit_l as the top encoders and transformer as the best aggregation. The remaining untested scvi_n200 + multiprofile configs all use avgpool, which underperformed transformer (config_004: 0.7062 vs config_012: 0.7250). Question: config_034 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + concat) is the highest-expected-accuracy untested config, pairing the two best encoders with avgpool and concat fusion. It tests whether concat fusion with the best encoders can narrow the gap to the transformer baseline. Why this is the best last experiment: No untested config is likely to exceed 0.7250 given the strong evidence, but config_034 has the highest ceiling among remaining options since it retains both top encoders. Its expected cost (~4–5 GPU hours, comparable to config_004's 4.82) is moderate, and it provides a useful lower-bound confirmation of the transformer aggregation advantage without the higher cost of resnet50-based alternatives."
}

